.TH GIRLSERVE 1 2026-10-21 girlpages "girlpages Manual"
.SH NAME
girlserve \- serve a published girlpages site
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B girlserve
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-archive
.I dir
.br
.B girlserve
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-dir
.I site
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B girlserve
serves a girlpages site (its website and its repository) as
.B girlrepo publish
made it: from an archive, as
.B girlrepo publish \-\-archive
writes, or from a site directory.
It's
.B girlrepo serve
on its own, for production: a small static program with nothing else in
it, for a minimal container image.
.PP
Each file is sent in the smallest form the client accepts (zstd, brotli,
gzip or as it is, by its
.BR Accept-Encoding ),
with the
.B Cache-Control
of its kind (immutable for files named after their hash, five minutes for
the files that point to them, an hour for the website, and no-cache for its
service worker), a strong
.B ETag
(from an archive; a directory's files get
.B Last-Modified
instead), range requests, and the site's own 404 page.
.PP
An archive is checked for a new version every
.B \-\-reload-interval
and on
.BR SIGHUP ;
a new one is loaded alongside what's being served and switched to at once,
so no request sees half of each.
If it can't be loaded, what was being served still is, and it's tried again
next time.
Until the archive has a version (before its first publish), every request
gets 503 and
.B /readyz
fails.
.PP
On
.B SIGTERM
or
.BR SIGINT ,
.B /readyz
fails at once, the site is served for
.B \-\-drain-delay
more (so load balancers notice first), and then requests in flight get
.B \-\-drain
to finish.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-archive =\fIdir\fR
Serve the archive in
.I dir
(or
.BR $GIRLSERVE_ARCHIVE ).
It may be on a network file system: only a few files are opened, and each
request is a read of the bytes it sends.
.TP
.BR \-\-dir =\fIsite\fR
Serve a site directory instead.
.TP
.BR \-\-listen =\fIaddr\fR
Serve the site on
.I addr
(default
.BR :8080 ,
or
.BR $GIRLSERVE_LISTEN ).
.TP
.BR \-\-admin\-listen =\fIaddr\fR
Serve
.B /healthz
(the process is up),
.B /readyz
(it has a site to serve, and isn't stopping) and
.B /metrics
(Prometheus) on
.I addr
(default
.BR :9090 ,
or
.BR $GIRLSERVE_ADMIN_LISTEN ;
empty for none), which shouldn't be public.
.TP
.BR \-\-reload\-interval =\fIduration\fR
How often to check the archive for a new version (default 10s; 0 for only on
.BR SIGHUP ).
.TP
.B \-\-access\-log
Write a line of JSON for each request to standard output: its time, method,
path, status, size, duration, encoding, address, referrer and user agent.
.TP
.BR \-\-drain\-delay =\fIduration\fR
When stopping, keep serving this long first, with
.B /readyz
failing (default 5s).
.TP
.BR \-\-drain =\fIduration\fR
Then give requests in flight this long to finish (default 30s).
Packs are hundreds of megabytes, so there's no limit on how long a response
may take otherwise.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH METRICS
.TP
.B girlpages_http_requests_total{code}
Requests, by status.
.TP
.B girlpages_http_request_duration_seconds
How long they took (a histogram).
.TP
.B girlpages_http_response_bytes_total
Bytes of response bodies.
.TP
.BR girlpages_archive_generated_time_seconds ", " girlpages_archive_loaded_time_seconds
When the version being served was written, and loaded: alert on either
getting old.
.TP
.BR girlpages_archive_reloads_total ", " girlpages_archive_reload_failures_total
Reloads that changed what's served, and those that failed.
.TP
.BR girlpages_archive_files ", " girlpages_archive_live_bytes
The size of the version being served.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B girlserve \-\-archive /data/archive \-\-access\-log
Serve the archive the publishing job writes to, on :8080, with health and
metrics on :9090.
.PP
.B dist/hosting/kubernetes.yaml
in the source has a CronJob that unpacks packs dropped into a directory,
publishes them into an archive, and a Deployment of
.B girlserve
serving it.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR girlrepo (1),
.BR girl (1),
.BR girlc (1)
